{"node":{"id":"MONDO:0021081","label":"anti-NMDA receptor encephalitis","definition":"An autoimmune acute encephalitis caused by antibodies against the glutamate NMDA receptor. It usually affects females and in the majority of cases it is associated with the presence of a tumor, most commonly an ovarian teratoma. The presence of a tumor in patients with this form of encephalitis implies that the latter is a paraneoplastic syndrome. It is manifested with psychiatric symptoms and epileptic seizures. It is a potentially lethal disorder; however, it is usually reversible with the prompt removal of the tumor.","synonyms":["limbic encephalitis with N-methyl-D-aspartate receptor antibodies","limbic encephalitis with NMDA receptor antibodies"],"xrefs":["GARD:0020513","MEDGEN:458943","MESH:D060426","NANDO:2201317","NCIT:C94853","Orphanet:217253","SCTID:716684004","UMLS:C2986717","icd11.foundation:1568915618"],"parents":[],"parents_labels":{},"children":[],"children_labels":{},"in_core":false,"cluster_id":null,"is_group":false,"n_genes":0,"n_phenotypes":53,"mechanism_classes":[]},"genes":[],"phenotypes":[{"edge":{"id":"e_458d51ffc3a1","source":"MONDO:0021081","target":"HP:0032264","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:217253 · ORPHA:217253","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/217253","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"NMDA receptor encephalitis: Anti-NMDA receptor antibody positivity (frequency HP:0040281) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:217253","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/217253","confidence":0.9,"snippet":"Anti-NMDA receptor antibody positivity — Very frequent (99-80%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.9,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"phenotype":{"id":"HP:0032264","label":"Anti-NMDA receptor antibody positivity","ic":9.462}},{"edge":{"id":"e_cb0bb289ee29","source":"MONDO:002108